    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'agenda' primarily refers to a list of items to be discussed at a meeting or a plan of things to be done. While 日程 (nittei) can mean 'schedule' or 'program of events' (which can be an aspect of an agenda), it does not fully capture the core meaning of 'agenda' as 'topics for discussion'. For that, 議題 (gidai) is a much more precise and natural translation. Therefore, 日程 is semantically narrower, covering only the 'schedule/program' aspect.",
